        summary: "At 10:30 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} and a friend used a hacksaw and a pry bar at a town basketball court. The nets were cut from two hoops and one rim bent. The camera recorded the damage in fifteen minutes. The town replaced the nets and straightened the rim for $420. {D} says the nets were already torn.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Court Camera", "{D} cuts a net and pries a rim at 10:35 p.m."), E(.physical, 2, "Cut Nets", "Two nets with clean saw cuts and a rim bent forty degrees."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Invoice", "$420 for two nets and a rim repair."), E(.statement, 2, "Parks Worker", "The nets were intact at the afternoon inspection.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Already Torn", "{DL} says the nets were already torn and {D.he} only pulled them down."), E(.document, 1, "Work Order", "A work order to inspect the nets the week before.")],
        role: "Parks worker",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find at the town basketball court?", "\"Two nets cut from two hoops and one rim bent about forty degrees. The camera recorded it over fifteen minutes.\""), .direct("What does the court camera show?", "\"{D} cutting a net and prying a rim at 10:35 p.m., with a friend nearby. They had a hacksaw and a pry bar.\""), .direct("What did the repairs cost?", "\"$420 for two nets and a rim repair. The invoice is in our file.\""), .direct("How did you find the damage at the court?", "\"At about 7 a.m. I went to check the hoops and found two nets cut away and one rim bent down at an angle.\""), .direct("When had you last inspected the nets?", "\"The afternoon before. A work order was open to check them, and I inspected both hoops. The nets were hanging intact.\""), .direct("What did the camera show?", "\"At 10:35 p.m. a person with a saw cuts a net, and a second person works at a rim with a pry bar. The footage runs about fifteen minutes.\""), .cross("{D} says the nets were already torn, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A teen who plays there says they were frayed for weeks. But they were intact at my afternoon inspection.\""), .cross("How can you say the cuts are new?", "\"The nets have clean saw cuts, not wear. Frayed edges look different from saw marks.\""), .cross("Who had the saw?", "\"I have heard a friend carried it. I cannot say whose it was.\""), .cross("Were the nets in good shape before?", "\"They were worn at the edges but still in place. I would call them frayed, not torn through.\""), .cross("How can you be sure the cuts were not wear?", "\"Because the ends are clean and straight like a saw cut. Wear leaves jagged strands.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Teen who plays at the court",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Were the nets at the court torn before that night?", "\"Frayed at the edges for weeks. They were not whole, though I would not call them cut.\""), .direct("Who had the saw that night?", "\"A friend of {D}. I saw the friend carry a backpack, but I did not see the saw itself.\""), .direct("Did you see the rim after it was bent?", "\"Yes. I saw it bent the next day. It was bent about forty degrees, and it stayed that way.\""), .direct("How often do you play at that court?", "\"Several times a week. I know the regulars and the court's condition.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the nets before that night?", "\"The edges were frayed for weeks and some strands hung down. One looked like it would tear off soon.\""), .direct("What did you see the next day?", "\"The nets were gone and a rim was bent. The ends of the net cords looked sawed.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} cut anything?", "\"No. I was not there when it happened. I only saw the aftermath.\""), .cross("Were the nets cut cleanly or frayed through?", "\"I would say cut. The ends were clean. I did not want to say that earlier.\""), .cross("Do you know {D} well?", "\"I play at the court. I know {D} a little. I am telling you what I saw.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} do anything to the nets?", "\"No. I was not at the court when it happened.\""), .cross("Why do you think the nets were cut?", "\"I do not know. I only know they were worn before.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} cut the nets and bent a rim.", "The nets were already torn."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} carried the saw in a backpack.", "The nets were frayed and {DL} only pulled one down."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you cut the nets and bend the rim?", "\"I pulled down one net that was already torn. I did not cut two or bend a rim on purpose.\""), .direct("Why did you go to the court that night?", "\"To play and hang out with a friend. It was late, but the lights were on and the court was empty.\""), .direct("Who had the saw?", "\"My friend carried it in a backpack. I did not use it. I only pulled the net.\""), .direct("How often do you play at the court?", "\"Most evenings when it is not raining. A few of us shoot around after dinner.\""), .direct("What state were the nets in that night?", "\"One was frayed and hanging by a few strands. I tugged it down to keep it from tangling and handed it to my friend.\""), .direct("Where did the saw and pry bar come from?", "\"My friend had a backpack with tools. I did not ask why. I did not use them to damage anything on purpose.\""), .cross("The camera shows you cutting a net, doesn't it?", "\"It shows someone with a saw. My friend had the saw. I pulled one net.\""), .cross("The nets were intact at the afternoon inspection, weren't they?", "\"They were frayed. Frayed is not intact. I pulled one that was nearly down.\""), .cross("A rim bent forty degrees did not happen by itself. Who did that?", "\"It happened when we were hanging on it. I did not mean to bend it.\""), .cross("The video shows you working at a rim with a pry bar. Why?", "\"I tried to straighten a bend that I thought we caused hanging on it. I should have left it.\""), .cross("The town's inspection said the nets were intact. Who is right?", "\"They looked at it in the afternoon. By night the nets were worse. I do not think they were fully intact.\"")],
        openings: ("At 10:30 p.m., a court camera shows {D} and a friend with a hacksaw and a pry bar at a town basketball court. Two nets were cut and a rim bent, and the repairs cost $420.", "The defense evidence will establish that the nets were frayed for weeks, that a friend carried the saw, and that {D} only pulled down one net."),
        closings: ("Clean saw cuts, a bent rim, and a camera showing {D} at the hoops with tools. The nets were intact at the afternoon inspection.", "Frayed nets, a friend with a saw, and one net pulled down. The State must prove {D} cut and bent what was damaged, and a friend's saw is not {D}'s."),
        timeline: [(0, "Afternoon: the parks worker inspects the court."), (0, "10:35 p.m.: {D} cuts the net."), (0, "10:50 p.m.: the teens leave."), (1, "The parks worker finds the damage.")],
        identified: "The court camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The friend with the saw was never identified.", "The nets' replacement order was never checked."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let lockChangeBelongingsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.lockChangeBelongings",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Property Manager Enters Apartment With Master Key and Moves Furniture to Curb", "Tenant Returns From Work to Find Belongings on the Sidewalk"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a tenant, without legal authority, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "While {V} was at work on {DATE}, {D}, the property manager, used a master key to enter {V}'s apartment at 10 a.m. {D} carried a couch, a bed frame and boxes to the curb. {V} returned at 5 p.m. and found the belongings on the sidewalk in light rain. No eviction order existed and the lease requires 24 hours of written notice. {D} says rent was a month late.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Building Camera", "{D} carries furniture from {V}'s unit to the curb between 10:10 and 11:30 a.m."), E(.document, 3, "Lease Clause", "Section 14 requires 24 hours of written notice before entry."), E(.document, 2, "Key Log", "The master key was signed out by {D} at 9:55 a.m."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "Received no notice and found belongings in the rain.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Month Late", "{DL} says rent was a month late and the unit was abandoned."), E(.document, 1, "Rent Ledger", "A balance of $1,100 unpaid for thirty-five days.")],
        role: "Tenant",
        exam: [.direct("What did you find when you came home at 5 p.m.?", "\"My belongings on the sidewalk in light rain. A couch, a bed frame, and boxes had been carried to the curb.\""), .direct("How did they get there?", "\"The building camera shows {D}, the property manager, carrying furniture from my unit between 10:10 and 11:30 a.m.\""), .direct("What notice did you receive?", "\"None. The lease requires 24 hours of written notice before entry, and I got nothing. No eviction order existed.\""), .direct("What did you see when you got home at 5 p.m.?", "\"A couch, a bed frame, and boxes stacked on the wet sidewalk under a drizzle. My mattress was soaked through and my papers were ruined.\""), .direct("What did the building camera show?", "\"{D} unlocking my door with a key at 10:10 and carrying furniture to the curb for about eighty minutes. {D} left the door open.\""), .direct("What did the lease say about entry?", "\"Section 14 requires 24 hours of written notice before entering. I never received anything. No eviction had been filed either.\""), .cross("{D} says your rent was a month late, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. I was late. I do not dispute that. But late rent does not allow a manager to throw out my belongings.\""), .cross("Did {D} talk to you before that day?", "\"About the rent, yes. Not about clearing my unit.\""), .cross("Was your unit occupied?", "\"Yes. I live there. I work long shifts, so it often looks empty during the day.\""), .cross("Were you behind on rent?", "\"Yes, $1,100 for about five weeks. I had told the office I was working to catch up.\""), .cross("Did the unit look abandoned?", "\"I work long shifts and am rarely home during the day. I suppose a stranger might think so, but my things were all there.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Other tenant in the building",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did the manager give notice to anyone in the building?", "\"Not to me. I never got a written notice before the manager entered my unit, either.\""), .direct("Has the manager cleared units before?", "\"Twice this year that I know of. Each time, the tenant had been late on rent.\""), .direct("Did you see {V}'s belongings on the curb?", "\"Yes. A couch and a bed frame and boxes were sitting in the rain. It looked terrible.\""), .direct("How long have you lived in the building?", "\"Three years. I know most of the tenants and the manager.\""), .direct("What did you see that morning?", "\"The manager pulled a hand truck down the hall and carried furniture out of a unit to the curb. I thought it was a move-out.\""), .direct("What have you seen the manager do with units before?", "\"Two tenants in the last year were cleared out after leaving. Each time there was some kind of notice, I think.\""), .cross("Was {V}'s unit empty when the manager entered?", "\"No. I do not think so. {V} lived there, and the furniture was inside.\""), .cross("Did you hear the manager say anything about it?", "\"I heard that the unit would be cleared out. I did not hear it directly.\""), .cross("Do you know whether {V} was behind on rent?", "\"I heard so. I do not know how far.\""), .cross("Did you know {V}'s unit was occupied?", "\"I knew {V} lived there. I did not know the rent status.\""), .cross("Did you talk to the manager that day?", "\"Briefly. The manager said the unit was being cleared out and that {V} was gone.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} entered and removed a tenant's things without authority.", "{D} cleared a unit that looked abandoned."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had told another tenant the unit would be 'cleared out.'", "The unit looked empty because {V} worked long shifts."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you enter {V}'s apartment?", "\"Rent was a month late, and I believed the unit was empty. I used the master key to check.\""), .direct("Why did you move the furniture to the curb?", "\"I thought {V} had abandoned the unit. It looked empty during the day, and I wanted to re-rent it.\""), .direct("Did you give notice?", "\"No. I did not give 24 hours' written notice. I should have, and I know that now.\""), .direct("How long have you managed the building?", "\"Four years. I collect rent, handle repairs, and show vacant units.\""), .direct("What led you to think the unit was abandoned?", "\"The rent was thirty-five days late and I did not see {V} for weeks. I knocked several times and left notes with no response.\""), .direct("Why did you move the belongings?", "\"I wanted to re-rent the unit and thought the tenant had left. I carried the furniture out so cleaners could work.\""), .cross("You signed out the master key at 9:55 a.m. and carried out furniture for over an hour, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did. I was wrong to do that.\""), .cross("You told another tenant the unit would be 'cleared out.' What did you mean?", "\"I meant I thought it was empty. I did not know {V} still lived there.\""), .cross("{V}'s belongings sat in the rain for hours. Do you accept that?", "\"Yes. I feel awful about it. It was my mistake.\""), .cross("Did you check with {V} or the owner before moving anything?", "\"No. I should have called. I acted on my own.\""), .cross("A court order is required to remove a tenant. Why skip it?", "\"I was under pressure to fill units, and I let that push me past the rules.\"")],
        openings: ("While {V} was at work, {D}, the property manager, used a master key to enter {V}'s apartment and carried a couch, a bed frame, and boxes to the curb. The lease required 24 hours' written notice, and no eviction order existed.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {V}'s rent was a month late, that the unit looked empty, and that {D} believed it had been abandoned."),
        closings: ("A master key signed out at 9:55, furniture carried to the curb in the rain, no notice, and no eviction order. A landlord cannot clear a tenant's home on a manager's own authority.", "A late rent, a unit that looked empty, and a manager who believed it was abandoned. A mistake about occupancy is not a criminal intent to steal."),
        timeline: [(0, "9:55 a.m.: {D} signs out the master key."), (0, "10:10 a.m.: {D} enters the unit."), (0, "5 p.m.: {V} comes home."), (1, "The building sends its camera video.")],
        identified: "The key log and the camera identify {D}.",
        notDone: ["The manager's key log for other entries was never reviewed.", "No one asked whether the unit had been posted before entry."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let plowSmashV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.plowSmash",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Loader Backs Into Delivery Vans and Cars in Apartment Lot at 5 a.m.", "Contract Dispute Ends With Bucket Through Parked Vehicles"],
        law: "injuryPersonalProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured personal property of {V}, parked vehicles, causing damage of $2,600, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, a plowing contractor for an apartment complex, was told the day before {DATE} that the contract would end because of unpaid bills. At 5 a.m. {D} drove a front-end loader into the lot and backed the bucket into two delivery vans and a parked car. {V}, who owns the vans, found the damage at 6 a.m. The repairs came to $2,600. {D} says the loader slid on ice.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Lot Camera", "A loader backs into three parked vehicles at 5:04 a.m. and keeps backing."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimates", "$2,600 for two vans and a car."), E(.document, 2, "Termination Notice", "A notice ending {D}'s plowing contract the day before."), E(.statement, 2, "{V}", "Saw the loader leave and found the damage at 6 a.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Slid on Ice", "{DL} says the loader slid on the ice."), E(.document, 1, "Weather Record", "Freezing drizzle between 3 and 6 a.m.")],
        role: "Delivery van owner",
        exam: [.direct("What do you own that was damaged?", "\"Two delivery vans. A parked car was hit too. The repairs came to $2,600 for the three vehicles.\""), .direct("What did your lot camera show?", "\"A loader backing into three parked vehicles at 5:04 a.m. and continuing to back after it hit them.\""), .direct("What had happened the day before?", "\"The plowing contract had been ended by a termination notice because of unpaid bills. {D} was the plowing contractor.\""), .direct("What did you find at 6 a.m.?", "\"Both of my delivery vans with crushed rear doors and a parked car with a smashed side. The lot was icy and one van was pushed several feet.\""), .direct("What did the camera show?", "\"A front-end loader backing across the lot at 5:04 and striking all three vehicles. It kept backing after the first impact and then drove off.\""), .direct("What did the repairs cost?", "\"$2,600 total. The vans were out of service for a week, and I lost deliveries.\""), .cross("{D} says the loader slid on ice, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. The lot was icy that morning. I will agree to that.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} hit the vans?", "\"No. I was not there. I only saw the loader leaving and found the damage at 6 a.m.\""), .cross("Did the loader keep backing after the first hit?", "\"The camera shows it continuing to back. That is what concerns me.\""), .cross("Was the lot slick that morning?", "\"Yes. There was freezing drizzle overnight. I do not deny ice.\""), .cross("Do you know who operated the loader?", "\"I only know what the camera and the manager said. The loader belongs to {D}.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Tenant of the complex",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Was the lot icy that morning?", "\"Freezing drizzle. The whole lot had a glaze on it. I slipped on my way to the car.\""), .direct("Did you hear the loader that morning?", "\"Backing up and beeping. I heard it clearly from my window, and it did not sound controlled.\""), .direct("Did you see the loader hit anything?", "\"No. I only heard it. I did not look out until it was over.\""), .direct("How long have you lived in the complex?", "\"Five years. My window faces the lot, and I hear the plow before work.\""), .direct("What was the weather that morning?", "\"Freezing drizzle from around three. By five there was a glaze on everything.\""), .direct("What did you hear?", "\"A loader backing with the alarm beeping and a loud crunch. I did not look out right away.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} in the cab before the hit?", "\"No. I did not see anyone in the cab. I only heard the machine.\""), .cross("Did you hear anything about the contract ending?", "\"I heard {D} was upset about it.\""), .cross("Was the loader's back-up alarm working?", "\"Yes. It was beeping the whole time.\""), .cross("Did you see who was driving?", "\"No. I did not see anyone in the cab.\""), .cross("Did you notice the loader slide?", "\"I heard it grind, but I could not tell if it slid.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} rammed parked vehicles after losing the contract.", "{D} lost control on ice."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry. It won't happen again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had told a tenant the contract end would 'cost them.'", "The lot was icy and the loader's brakes were weak."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you hit the vans on purpose?", "\"No. The loader slid on ice, and I could not stop it. I did not plan to hit anything.\""), .direct("Why were you at the lot at 5 a.m.?", "\"I came to plow, as I have for years. I did not know I would be treated as finished.\""), .direct("What about the termination notice?", "\"I got it the day before. I was upset, but I would never wreck vehicles over it.\""), .direct("How long had you plowed this complex?", "\"Six years. I come out at five after storms and clear the lot before tenants leave.\""), .direct("How did you feel after the termination notice?", "\"Angry and worried. I had equipment payments and thought the complex would pay what it owed.\""), .direct("What happened with the loader that morning?", "\"I came to plow and backed up to turn. The lot was a sheet of ice, and the loader slid back when I hit the brakes.\""), .cross("You told a tenant the end of the contract would 'cost them,' didn't you?", "\"I said something like that out of frustration. I did not mean it literally.\""), .cross("The loader kept backing after hitting the first van, didn't it?", "\"The brakes were weak, and the ice made it slide. I could not control it.\""), .cross("Three vehicles were hit. Do you accept responsibility?", "\"I do. I truly am sorry. I did not intend it.\""), .cross("The camera shows you continuing to back after the first hit. Why?", "\"The brakes were weak, and I could not stop it. I tried several times.\""), .cross("You told a tenant that ending the contract would cost them. Isn't that a threat?", "\"It was frustration. I did not mean to hit any cars.\"")],
        openings: ("A day after a plowing contract was ended over unpaid bills, {D} drove a front-end loader into an apartment lot at 5 a.m. and backed the bucket into two delivery vans and a car. The damage came to $2,600.", "The defense will present evidence that the lot was glazed with ice, that the loader's brakes were weak, and that {D} slid into the vehicles by accident."),
        closings: ("A fired contractor, a loader at 5 a.m., three vehicles hit, and a machine that kept backing after the first impact. That is not a slip.", "A lot glazed with ice and a loader with weak brakes. The State must prove {D} hit those vehicles on purpose, and the weather raises real doubt."),
        timeline: [(-1, "The complex ends {D}'s contract."), (0, "5:04 a.m.: the loader backs into the vehicles."), (0, "6 a.m.: {V} finds the damage."), (1, "The vehicle owners get estimates.")],
        identified: "The lot camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The loader's brakes were never tested.", "The termination notice was never shown to {DL}'s employer."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let trashCanBlazeV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.trashCanBlaze",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Dumpster Fire Lit Against Church Wall at 1 a.m.", "Lighter Fluid Can Found Near Scorched Brick"],
        law: "injuryRealProperty",
        spec: "Willfully and wantonly injured real property of {V}, a church, causing damage of $2,400, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 1:05 a.m. on {DATE}, {D} pushed a dumpster against the brick wall of a church and lit it. The fire crept up the wall and scorched the brick and a window frame before an alarm company called the fire department at 1:20 a.m. The church paid $2,400 for repairs. {D} says {D.he} was burning trash to stay warm.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Church Lot Camera", "{D} pushes the dumpster to the wall and lights it at 1:05 a.m."), E(.physical, 2, "Lighter Fluid Can", "A half-empty can found in the lot."), E(.document, 2, "Fire Report", "Accelerant odor at the origin and scorching up the wall."), E(.document, 2, "Repair Estimate", "$2,400 for brick cleaning and a window frame.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Staying Warm", "{DL} says {D.he} was burning trash to keep warm."), E(.document, 1, "Weather Record", "A low of 28 degrees that night.")],
        role: "Church custodian",
        exam: [.direct("What did you see on your church lot camera?", "\"At 1:05 a.m., {D} pushed a dumpster against the brick wall of the church and lit it.\""), .direct("What damage did the fire do?", "\"It scorched the brick and a window frame before an alarm company called the fire department at 1:20. The church paid $2,400 to repair it.\""), .direct("What was found in the lot?", "\"A half-empty can of lighter fluid. The fire report found accelerant odor at the origin.\""), .direct("How did you learn of the fire?", "\"The alarm company called me at 1:20 a.m. after a motion and heat alert. I drove over and found firefighters hosing the wall.\""), .direct("What did the lot camera show?", "\"At about 1:05 {D} shoves a dumpster against the brick wall, squirts something on it, and lights it. The flames spread to the wall.\""), .direct("What damage did the fire cause?", "\"Scorched brick, a cracked window pane, and a melted window frame. Cleaning and repair came to $2,400.\""), .cross("{D} says {D.he} was burning trash to stay warm, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. It was 28 degrees that night. I will say it was bitterly cold.\""), .cross("Had {D} slept behind the church before?", "\"Yes, I had told {D} not to sleep there. I did not call anyone, though.\""), .cross("Did {D} flee?", "\"No. {D} stayed nearby. I do not know where {D} went afterward.\""), .cross("Did {D} stay or run?", "\"{D} walked off to the street and stayed in sight. Deputies found {D} a few blocks away.\""), .cross("Was anyone inside the building?", "\"No. The church was empty, but the sanctuary shares a wall with that side.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Shelter outreach worker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Was it cold that night?", "\"28 degrees. Anyone outside without shelter was in real danger from the cold.\""), .direct("Did you know {D}?", "\"I knew {D} as someone who sleeps behind buildings downtown. I have talked to {D} several times.\""), .direct("Did {D} have shelter that night?", "\"No. {D} had no home, and the shelter was full that week. {D} was out on the street.\""), .direct("What do you do as an outreach worker?", "\"I walk the streets at night and offer blankets, hot drinks, and rides to shelters for people sleeping outside.\""), .direct("What was the weather like that week?", "\"A hard cold snap. It dropped to 28 degrees, and our shelter beds were full.\""), .direct("What can you tell the jury about {D}?", "\"{D} is polite, quiet, and sleeps in alleys. {D} has refused beds when they were full and kept to the edges.\""), .cross("Did {D} mean to burn the church wall?", "\"I cannot say. I only know {D} was cold and had no place to go.\""), .cross("Would a fire against a church wall be dangerous?", "\"Yes. It could spread. I would never tell someone to do it.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} that night?", "\"No. I only know about the weather and {D}'s situation.\""), .cross("Did you speak with {D} that night?", "\"No. I came by after the fire. I did not see {D} then.\""), .cross("Would you ever suggest a person light a fire for warmth?", "\"No. We tell people not to. It is dangerous.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} lit a dumpster against a wall.", "{D} was keeping warm."),
        allocution: "\"I knew it wasn't mine. I'll pay it back.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been told by the custodian not to sleep behind the church.", "{DL} had no home and the fire got out of hand."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you light the dumpster?", "\"Yes. I pushed it against the wall to block the wind and lit it to stay warm. I did not mean to burn the church.\""), .direct("Why were you behind the church?", "\"I had nowhere else to go. It was 28 degrees, and the shelter was full. I thought the wall would block the wind.\""), .direct("Where did you get the lighter fluid?", "\"From a store. I used it to start the fire, and I did not think about how it would catch.\""), .direct("What was your night like?", "\"I was outside with no shelter. The temperature dropped to 28 and I was shivering behind the church.\""), .direct("Why did you push the dumpster?", "\"I wanted a windbreak. The wall of the church blocked the breeze, and the dumpster cut it more.\""), .direct("How did the fire start?", "\"I lit some trash for warmth and used lighter fluid I had to start it. It caught and climbed the wall before I could put it out.\""), .cross("The custodian had told you not to sleep behind the church, hadn't the custodian?", "\"Yes, I was told. I was desperate, and I came back anyway.\""), .cross("The fire got out of hand, didn't it?", "\"Yes. It crept up the wall. I panicked and left.\""), .cross("$2,400 in damage to a church. Do you accept that?", "\"Yes. I apologize. I did not mean to hurt anyone.\""), .cross("You were told not to sleep behind the church. Why come back?", "\"Because I had no place to go. I know that is not an excuse.\""), .cross("You put fire next to a church wall. Weren't you afraid of that?", "\"I was afraid when it spread. I tried to stamp it out and then ran for help.\"")],
        openings: ("At 1:05 a.m., {D} pushed a dumpster against the brick wall of a church and lit it. The fire scorched the brick and a window frame before the fire department arrived, and the church paid $2,400.", "The defense witnesses will explain that it was 28 degrees, that {D} had no shelter and lit the fire to stay warm, and that the fire got out of hand."),
        closings: ("A dumpster pushed against a church wall, lit with lighter fluid at 1 a.m., and a scorched wall. {D} had been told not to sleep behind the church.", "A freezing night, a person with no home, and a fire that got out of hand. The State must prove {D} meant to burn the wall, and desperation is not malice."),
        timeline: [(0, "1:05 a.m.: {D} lights the dumpster."), (0, "1:20 a.m.: the alarm company calls the fire department."), (0, "1:45 a.m.: the fire is out."), (1, "The church gets repair estimates.")],
        identified: "The lot camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The shelter's availability that night was never confirmed.", "The accelerant odor was never tested against a fuel source."],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let aideCashV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.aideCash",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Birthday Card Cash Disappears From Assisted Living Closet", "Night Aide Takes $300 From Resident's Coat Pocket"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a resident of an assisted living home, valued at $300, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{V} received a birthday card holding $300 on {DATE} and hung the coat holding it in the closet of an assisted living room. The night aide, {D}, entered the room at 2:15 a.m. for a check and spent four minutes inside. At breakfast the cash was gone from the coat pocket. {D} says {V} gave {D.him} a tip months earlier and that the coat was not touched.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hallway Camera", "{D} enters {V}'s room at 2:15 a.m. and leaves at 2:19 a.m. with a hand in a pocket."), E(.document, 2, "Visitor Log", "The birthday card was left by a visitor at 5 p.m. with an envelope of cash."), E(.statement, 2, "Resident", "The cash was in the coat pocket when {V} went to bed."), E(.document, 2, "Shift Sheet", "{D} was the only aide on the hall that night.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Old Tip", "{DL} says {V} slipped {D.him} money before and may have given it again."), E(.document, 1, "Room Check Log", "A routine check at 2:15 a.m. signed by {D}.")],
        role: "Assisted living resident",
        exam: [.direct("What did you receive on {DATE}?", "\"A birthday card holding $300. It was left by a visitor at 5 p.m., and I hung my coat with the cash in the closet.\""), .direct("What happened that night?", "\"I went to bed with the cash in my coat pocket. At breakfast I checked, and it was gone.\""), .direct("Who came into your room?", "\"The night aide, {D}, came at 2:15 a.m. for a check and spent four minutes inside. The camera shows {D} leaving with a hand in a pocket.\""), .direct("Who left the card and what was in it?", "\"A visitor left it at about 5 p.m. with an envelope of $300 in cash. I put it in my coat pocket and hung the coat in the closet.\""), .direct("How did you find out the money was gone?", "\"At breakfast I reached into the coat and the envelope was empty. I told the staff and they called a supervisor.\""), .direct("What do you remember of that night?", "\"I slept well. I woke at 2:15 when the aide came in for a room check, then went back to sleep.\""), .cross("{DL} says you gave {D.him} money before, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"I may have given a tip once, months ago. That doesn't mean I gave $300 that night.\""), .cross("Did you see {DL} take the cash?", "\"No. I was asleep. I only know it was there at bedtime and gone at breakfast.\""), .cross("Could the visitor have moved the cash?", "\"I suppose it's possible. But I put it in the coat myself.\""), .cross("Did the visitor move the envelope?", "\"A visitor came in the morning. I think the envelope might have been moved to the dresser, but I am not sure.\""), .cross("Do you remember tipping the aide in the past?", "\"Once, a small amount, many months ago. It was a thank-you.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Day-shift aide",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you work with {DL}?", "\"Yes. I'm a day-shift aide. I see {D} at shift change.\""), .direct("How is {DL} as an aide?", "\"Reliable and gentle with residents. I've never had any concerns.\""), .direct("Did residents give {DL} gifts?", "\"Sometimes small tips. Some residents like to. It's against policy, but it happens.\""), .direct("How long have you worked at the facility?", "\"Five years on the day shift. I know most of the aides and the night routine.\""), .direct("What kind of aide is {D}?", "\"Kind and patient. I never saw {D} take anything, and residents trust {D}.\""), .direct("What is the facility's policy on tips?", "\"We are not supposed to accept gifts. Some residents press small amounts on us anyway, and most of us decline.\""), .cross("Who else could enter the room?", "\"Visitors and staff in the morning. I can't say who was in it overnight.\""), .cross("Did you check the coat?", "\"No. I never saw it. I only heard about it.\""), .cross("Did you see anything that night?", "\"No. I was off shift. I only know the setup of the hall.\""), .cross("Who had access to {V}'s room in the morning?", "\"Staff and visitors. The door was often open at breakfast.\""), .cross("You were not on shift with {D} at 2:15 that night, were you?", "\"No. I work days and only know what the night log shows. I cannot tell you what happened inside that room.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took $300 from a sleeping resident's coat.", "A routine check and an old tip."),
        allocution: "\"I knew it wasn't mine. I'll pay it back.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} deposited $300 in cash two days later.", "The envelope was moved to a dresser by a visitor in the morning."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you enter {V}'s room at 2:15?", "\"It was a routine room check. I'm required to look in on residents. I signed the log, and I was in and out in a few minutes.\""), .direct("Did you take the cash?", "\"No. I didn't touch the coat. I never looked in a pocket. I would never take money from a resident.\""), .direct("Why was your hand in your pocket?", "\"I was holding my pen and keys. I put my hands in my pockets often.\""), .direct("What was your shift that night?", "\"Overnight on the hall with eight residents. I checked each room every two hours.\""), .direct("What did you do in {V}'s room at 2:15?", "\"I checked the call light, adjusted the blanket, and looked at the bathroom. It takes a few minutes with all the equipment.\""), .direct("What was the habit with your pocket?", "\"I carry a pen and keys and keep my hand on them in the dark. The camera shows a hand in a pocket.\""), .cross("You were the only aide on the hall, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I was alone on that hall. That's why I'm the one they point at.\""), .cross("You were in the room four minutes, weren't you?", "\"About that. A room check takes a few minutes, with the blanket and the call button.\""), .cross("{V} says you got a tip before, didn't {V.he}?", "\"Once, months ago, a small one. I didn't take any more than that.\""), .cross("You were alone on the hall. Who else could have gone into the coat?", "\"Anyone who came in during the night or morning. I did not touch the coat.\""), .cross("Nobody was with you in the room. Isn't it your word against {V}'s?", "\"It is my word, and I understand that. I did my check and left, and I never touched the coat.\"")],
        openings: ("A resident put $300 in a coat pocket after a birthday card arrived, and at breakfast it was gone. The night aide, {D}, entered the room at 2:15 a.m. and left four minutes later with a hand in a pocket. The State will show the camera and the shift sheet.", "Jurors will also see a routine room check that {D} signed, an aide who was the only one on the hall because staffing was thin, and a resident who once gave tips."),
        closings: ("The cash was in the coat at bedtime and gone at breakfast, and {D} was the only aide who entered that room overnight, with a hand in a pocket.", "A routine check and a coat nobody examined. The State has not proved {D} took anything, and a visitor may have moved the envelope."),
        timeline: [(0, "5:00 p.m.: a visitor leaves the card with $300."), (0, "2:15 a.m.: {D} enters the room."), (0, "2:19 a.m.: {D} leaves."), (0, "7:30 a.m.: {V} finds the pocket empty.")],
        identified: "The shift sheet and the hallway camera identify {D}.",
        notDone: ["The visitor who left the card was never asked what happened to the envelope.", "The coat was never checked for fingerprints."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let vapeGrabV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.vapeGrab",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Teen Grabs Two Cartons of Cigarettes and Jumps Into Waiting Car", "Gas Station Camera Shows Plate on Getaway Car"],
        law: "larcenyMerchant",
        spec: "Took merchandise valued at $340 from {V}, a gas station, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "At 9:40 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} walked into a gas station, grabbed two cartons of cigarettes from behind the counter while the clerk made change and ran to a waiting car. The camera caught the plate. The cartons cost $340. {D} says a friend dared {D.him} and {D.he} returned one carton the next day.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Store Camera", "{D} grabs two cartons and runs to a waiting car at 9:42 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Plate Record", "The getaway car's plate is registered to a friend of {D}."), E(.document, 2, "Inventory Count", "Two cartons missing from the counter display."), E(.statement, 2, "Clerk", "Was making change and turned back to an empty rack.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Dare", "{DL} says a friend dared {D.him}."), E(.document, 1, "Return Note", "A note left at the door the next day with one carton.")],
        role: "Gas station clerk",
        exam: [.direct("What happened at your counter at 9:40 p.m.?", "\"While I was making change, {D} grabbed two cartons of cigarettes from behind the counter and ran out to a waiting car.\""), .direct("What were the cartons worth?", "\"$340. The inventory count shows two cartons missing from the counter display.\""), .direct("Where were you standing and what happened?", "\"Behind the counter making change for a customer at 9:40. I heard the bell on the door and turned back to find two cartons gone.\""), .direct("What did the camera show?", "\"{D} reaching over the counter display, grabbing two cartons, and running out to a car idling in the lot. The plate is visible.\""), .direct("What did you do?", "\"I ran to the door and saw the car pulling away. I called deputies and gave them the plate.\""), .direct("What did you do after the car left the lot?", "\"I hit the alarm and gave the plate number to the sheriff's office. I locked the register, and I stayed inside until deputies arrived.\""), .cross("{D} says a friend dared {D.him}, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"That is what {D} says. The car was registered to a friend of {D}.\""), .cross("Did {D} return one carton?", "\"Yes. One was left at the door the next day, I understand.\""), .cross("Did {D} threaten you?", "\"No. {D} did not say anything. {D} just grabbed and ran.\""), .cross("Did {D} say anything?", "\"No. {D} did not speak and did not touch me or threaten me.\""), .cross("How do you know the carton came back?", "\"A note and one carton were left at the door the next day. The note said sorry.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Friend who drove",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Whose idea was it to take the cartons?", "\"A dare from the group. We were all talking and egging each other on, and I do not remember who said it first.\""), .direct("Did {D} return one carton?", "\"Yes. {D} left it at the store's door the next day. I drove {D} there.\""), .direct("Did you wait in the car?", "\"Yes. I waited in the car while {D} went in. I did not go inside the store.\""), .direct("How do you know {D}?", "\"We are close friends. We grew up in the same neighborhood and spend a lot of time together.\""), .direct("What happened in the car before the store?", "\"We talked about dares. I teased {D} about not having the nerve and urged it on.\""), .direct("What did you do when {D} came out?", "\"{D} jumped in and told me to go. I hit the gas without thinking.\""), .cross("Did you plan the grab before you got there?", "\"We talked about it. I will not say we did not. It was an idea that grew.\""), .cross("Did you urge {D} to do it?", "\"I may have. I laughed and said go for it. I regret that.\""), .cross("Did you plan the grab?", "\"We talked about it for days, joking around. I did not know {D} would really do it.\""), .cross("Did you tell {D} to stop?", "\"No. I laughed along. I regret that.\""), .cross("You were behind the wheel and did not go into the store, did you?", "\"That is true. I stayed in the car. I should have told {D} to get back in the car, but I did not go inside.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} grabbed cartons and ran.", "{D} acted on a dare."),
        allocution: "\"I'm ashamed of it, Your Honor. I want to make it right.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had planned it for a week.", "The friend was the one who drove and urged it."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you grab the cartons?", "\"Yes, I did. A friend dared me, and I wanted to prove I could do it.\""), .direct("Why did you run?", "\"I knew it was wrong the moment I did it. I ran to the waiting car because I was scared.\""), .direct("Did you return anything?", "\"Yes. I returned one carton the next day by leaving it at the door.\""), .direct("How did the dare come about?", "\"We were hanging out and someone said I would not do it. I said I would, and we drove to the station.\""), .direct("What did you do at the counter?", "\"I waited until the clerk turned to make change, grabbed two cartons, and ran to the car.\""), .direct("What happened the next day?", "\"I felt awful and brought one carton back with a note. I kept the other because I had already given it away.\""), .cross("You had planned it for a week, hadn't you?", "\"We talked about it for a while. It was not a spur-of-the-moment thing.\""), .cross("The car that waited was your friend's, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. My friend drove. I am sorry I got my friend involved.\""), .cross("Two cartons, $340. Only one was returned. Where is the other?", "\"I do not have it. I will pay for it.\""), .cross("You and your friend talked about this for a week. Isn't that planning?", "\"We joked about it for a while. The dare came up that night, and I went along.\""), .cross("One carton is still missing. Will you pay for it?", "\"Yes. I will pay for the second carton. I should have done that at the start.\"")],
        openings: ("At 9:40 p.m., {D} grabbed two cartons of cigarettes worth $340 from behind a gas station counter and ran to a waiting car. The camera caught the plate, which belongs to a friend of {D}.", "The defense case is that {D} acted on a group dare, returned one carton the next day, regrets the whole thing, and is ready to pay for the other."),
        closings: ("Two cartons grabbed while the clerk made change, a run to a waiting car, and a plan that was a week in the making. {D} took what was not paid for.", "A dare among friends and a foolish grab. {D} returned a carton the next day and is ready to pay for the other, which calls for restitution."),
        timeline: [(0, "9:40 p.m.: {D} walks in."), (0, "9:42 p.m.: {D} grabs the cartons."), (0, "9:45 p.m.: the clerk calls deputies."), (1, "A carton is left at the door.")],
        identified: "The store camera and the plate identify {D}.",
        notDone: ["The driver was never charged or interviewed.", "The returned carton was never checked against the stock count."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let foodDriveBoxV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.foodDriveBox",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Pantry Shelf of Diapers and Formula Emptied the Night Before Distribution", "Church Hall Camera Shows Bag Filled With Baby Supplies"],
        law: "misdLarceny",
        spec: "Stole property of {V}, a church, valued at $130, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A church food pantry stocked diapers and infant formula on a shelf for its Saturday distribution on {DATE}. At 9 p.m. the night before, {D} entered the hall and filled a bag with diapers and four cans of formula. The pantry coordinator counted the shelf the next morning and found it nearly empty. {D} says {D.he} needed the supplies and meant to sign for them.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Hall Camera", "{D} fills a bag with diapers and formula at 9:05 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Stock Sheet", "Eight packs of diapers and six cans of formula counted at 6 p.m."), E(.document, 2, "Pantry Rules", "A posted rule that supplies are given only on distribution days with a sign-in."), E(.statement, 2, "Coordinator", "Counted the empty shelf at 8 a.m.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Needed Supplies", "{DL} says {D.he} needed diapers and formula for a baby."), E(.document, 1, "Sign-In Sheet", "{DL}'s name signed in at an earlier distribution day.")],
        role: "Church volunteer",
        exam: [.direct("What was on the pantry shelf on {DATE}?", "\"Eight packs of diapers and six cans of formula, counted at 6 p.m. for our Saturday distribution.\""), .direct("What does the hall camera show?", "\"At 9:05 p.m., {D} filled a bag with diapers and four cans of formula.\""), .direct("What did the coordinator find?", "\"The shelf nearly empty at 8 a.m. Our posted rule says supplies are given only on distribution days, with a sign-in.\""), .direct("How is the pantry organized for Saturday distribution?", "\"We stock a shelf in the fellowship hall with diapers, formula, and canned goods during the week. Clients sign in on Saturday, and volunteers hand out items by household size.\""), .direct("What did you count at 6 p.m. the night before?", "\"Eight packs of diapers and six cans of formula on the shelf. I wrote it on the stock sheet and locked the kitchen but left the hall door for the choir.\""), .direct("What did you see on the camera?", "\"At 9:05 p.m. {D} walks in, takes a bag from a cart, and fills it with diapers and four cans of formula. {D} leaves a few minutes later.\""), .cross("{DL} says {D.he} needed the supplies, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"We would have helped on distribution day. I can't judge anyone's need.\""), .cross("Did {DL} sign in before?", "\"I'm told so. {D} signed in at an earlier distribution day.\""), .cross("Did anyone offer {DL} an emergency pack?", "\"No. We don't have a formal process. I suppose someone could have been asked.\""), .cross("Did {D} try to hide?", "\"No. {D} walked in plainly, looked around, and took the items. It was not hurried.\""), .cross("Would the pantry have given {D} the supplies on Saturday?", "\"If {D} signed in and qualified, yes. We help families with babies every week.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Pantry client",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Do you use the pantry?", "\"Yes. I'm a client. I come on distribution days and sign in.\""), .direct("Have you seen {DL} there?", "\"Yes. {D} came to an earlier distribution day and signed in. {D} seemed polite.\""), .direct("Did {DL} talk about a baby?", "\"{D} mentioned needing diapers and formula. I felt for {D}.\""), .direct("How long have you been a pantry client?", "\"About eight months. I come every Saturday for diapers and food for my children.\""), .direct("What did you see of {D} at the pantry?", "\"{D} came to an earlier distribution day and quietly asked about diapers and formula. {D} seemed shy and tired.\""), .direct("What did {D} tell you about the baby?", "\"That the baby was a few months old and was on formula. {D} said money was tight.\""), .cross("Can you say {DL} was in need that week?", "\"Only what {D} told me. I don't know {D}'s situation.\""), .cross("Are supplies meant to be given out at night?", "\"No. They're for distribution day. That's the rule.\""), .cross("Did {DL} ask you for help?", "\"No. I wish {D} had. I would have tried to help.\""), .cross("Were you at the hall that night?", "\"No. I was home with my own children. I only know what happened from the camp talk.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever mention taking supplies without signing?", "\"No. If {D} had said that, I would have told {D} to ask the coordinator.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} took supplies before distribution.", "{D} needed supplies for a baby."),
        allocution: "\"It was a stupid decision and someone else paid for it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} sold two of the formula cans online.", "{DL} has a baby and was out of work that week."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you take the diapers and formula?", "\"I had a baby and ran out. I needed them that night, and I couldn't wait until Saturday.\""), .direct("Did you plan to sign for them?", "\"Yes. I meant to sign for them. I was in a hurry, and I took them without signing.\""), .direct("Why did you go at night?", "\"That was when I could get to the hall. I thought no one would mind, since I'd been there before.\""), .direct("What was going on with your family that week?", "\"I had a baby at home, and we ran out of formula on Thursday. Money was tight because my work hours had been cut.\""), .direct("How did you know the hall would be open?", "\"The choir was practicing, and the door was open. I walked in and saw the shelf.\""), .direct("What did you plan to do about signing?", "\"I meant to sign the sheet in the morning and explain. I took only what I needed for a few days.\""), .cross("The rule says supplies are only given on distribution days, doesn't it?", "\"Yes. I knew that. I was desperate.\""), .cross("You took four cans of formula, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I took what I needed for several days. I didn't think about the others waiting.\""), .cross("You didn't ask anyone first, did you?", "\"No. I didn't know who to call. I should have tried.\""), .cross("Why not wait until Saturday when you could sign in?", "\"The baby needed to eat that night. I could not wait a day.\""), .cross("You never asked anyone for emergency help. Why?", "\"I did not know whom to call and I was embarrassed. I should have found someone.\"")],
        openings: ("A church pantry counted eight packs of diapers and six cans of formula for its Saturday distribution. At 9:05 the night before, the hall camera shows {D} filling a bag, and by morning the shelf was nearly empty. The State will show the video and the stock sheet.", "The defense will point you to a person with a baby who had used the pantry before, who needed supplies that night, and who meant to sign for them."),
        closings: ("A posted rule, a stock count at 6, and {D} filling a bag at 9:05. The supplies were set aside for families waiting for Saturday.", "{D} took diapers and formula for a baby and meant to sign. The State has not proved {D} meant to steal rather than meet an urgent need."),
        timeline: [(0, "6 p.m.: the stock sheet is counted."), (0, "9:05 p.m.: {D} fills the bag."), (1, "8 a.m.: the coordinator finds the shelf empty."), (1, "The church sends its hall video.")],
        identified: "The hall camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["No one offered {DL} an emergency pack.", "The church never checked the sign-in log for need."],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

