        defendant: [.direct("Were you sick those three days?", "\"Yes. I had a bad cold and a fever. I went to the walk-in and was given the form.\""), .direct("Where did the form come from?", "\"The hospital gave it to me at a walk-in visit. I didn't look closely at the logo or number.\""), .direct("Did you make the form?", "\"No. I took what I was handed. I would never forge a form.\""), .direct("How did you feel during those three days?", "\"Awful, with a high fever and chills. I stayed in bed and drank fluids.\""), .direct("Where did you get the form?", "\"I walked into the hospital's urgent care on the first day. A staff member handed me a form and told me to fill it out.\""), .direct("Why did you buy cold medicine?", "\"On the second day I could not shake the cough. I went to the pharmacy and got medicine.\""), .cross("The hospital says it has no visit for you, doesn't it?", "\"That's what they say. I don't understand. I was there.\""), .cross("The patient number belongs to someone else, doesn't it?", "\"I didn't know that. I didn't check the number.\""), .cross("The logo is two years out of date, isn't it?", "\"I didn't notice. I was sick. I just wanted to hand in my note.\""), .cross("The form carries a patient number that is not yours. How can that be?", "\"I do not know. I did not read the number. I took the paper to work.\""), .cross("The logo is two years old. Could the hospital have handed you an old form?", "\"It could have. I did not notice the logo.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} missed three days of work and gave a warehouse supervisor a hospital discharge form, but the hospital says the patient number belongs to someone else, the logo is two years out of date, and {D} never visited. The State will show the form and the hospital records.", "The defense evidence includes a worker who really was sick, a coworker who saw the cold, and a form {D} says the hospital gave {D.him}."),
