        openings: ("Two packages worth $450 were addressed to {V}, who has no roommate. {D} told the desk clerk {D.he} was the roommate, signed for them, and carried them to the elevator at 2:10 p.m. The State will show the log and the lobby camera.", "The defense will present a neighbor who picked up a package before, an earlier text about a package, and a clerk who never checked. Listen closely to the witnesses."),
        closings: ("Two packages, a false claim of being a roommate, a signature that is not {V}'s, and two boxes carried away on camera. {D} took what was not {D}'s.", "{D} thought {V} had asked for the pickup, and a text mentioned a package. The State has not proved {D} meant to keep them."),
