        openings: ("At 7:15 p.m., {D} drove an ATV off a county road onto a public golf course, across two fairways, and within a few feet of four players on a green, tearing turf on the ninth fairway.", "The defense case is that the course is used as a cut-through, that the entrance sign was faded, and that {D} did not mean to endanger anyone."),
