        defendant: [.direct("Why did you stop walking the dog?", "\"I had a car accident on day four. I was shaken and unwell for days. I couldn't manage walks.\""), .direct("Why didn't you answer messages?", "\"I was overwhelmed. I'd lost my phone for part of it, and I didn't know what to say.\""), .direct("Did you mean to keep the $360?", "\"No. I meant to do the walks. Then everything fell apart. I should have contacted {V}.\""), .direct("What do you do for work?", "\"I care for pets while owners travel. I take clients by referral and rely on repeat business.\""), .direct("What happened on day four?", "\"I was in a minor collision in a parking lot. I was shaken and had a headache for days.\""), .direct("Why did you stop responding to messages?", "\"I felt guilty and overwhelmed. I lost my phone for part of that stretch and did not know how to explain.\""), .cross("You took $360 up front, didn't you?", "\"Yes. For a month. I only walked twice.\""), .cross("The dog went without water, didn't it?", "\"I know. I'm so sorry. That's on me.\""), .cross("You never refunded anything, did you?", "\"Not yet. I want to make it right.\""), .cross("You took $360 up front. How many walks did you do?", "\"Two. I should have refunded the rest.\""), .cross("You had other prepaid clients that month too. Did they get walks?", "\"I took on other work and fell behind everywhere. I am ashamed.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} paid {D} $360 for a month of weekday dog walks. {D} walked the dog twice, then stopped answering fourteen messages, and the dog was found in distress on day thirteen. The State will show the payment, the messages, and the camera.", "Jurors will also see a car accident on day four that left {D} shaken and unwell, a neighbor who saw it, and no plan to take the money."),
