        summary: "{D} settled into a hospital emergency waiting room chair at 11 p.m. on {DATE} with no patient to accompany. A security guard asked {D} to leave at midnight and again at 2 a.m. and cited the hospital policy that only patients and escorts may remain. {D} stayed until deputies came at 3:10 a.m. {D} says {D.he} was waiting for a ride.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Waiting Room Camera", "{D} sleeps in a chair from 11:20 p.m. until deputies arrive at 3:10 a.m."), E(.document, 3, "Hospital Policy", "Posted policy that only patients and escorts may remain overnight."), E(.statement, 2, "Security Guard", "Gave two warnings and was told no both times."), E(.document, 2, "Visitor Log", "No patient was registered under {D}'s name.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Waiting for a Ride", "{DL} says a ride was coming and the weather was bad."), E(.document, 1, "Weather Alert", "A freezing rain alert for the night.")],
        role: "Security guard",
        exam: [.direct("What is your job at the hospital, and were you working the night of {DATE}?", "\"I'm a contract security guard for the hospital, and I worked the overnight shift. My post covers the emergency entrance and the waiting room, so I walk through it about every half hour.\""), .direct("When did you first notice {D}?", "\"On my eleven-thirty round. {D} had settled into a chair near the vending machines with a jacket pulled up around {D.his} shoulders and appeared to be asleep. The camera has {D} there from 11:20.\""), .direct("What is the hospital policy about the waiting room at night?", "\"Overnight, only patients and one escort per patient may remain. It's posted by the triage window and printed on the visitor sign-in sheet. Everyone else is asked to wait outside or leave.\""), .direct("What did you say to {D} at midnight?", "\"I woke {D} gently, told {D.him} about the policy, and asked whether {D.he} was with a patient. {D} said no. I asked {D.him} to leave, and {D} said {D.he} was waiting on a ride.\""), .direct("What happened at two in the morning?", "\"I came back, and {D} was still in the same chair. I repeated the policy and asked again. {D} told me {D.he} would go when the ride came and stayed seated.\""), .direct("How did the deputies get involved?", "\"After the second refusal I called the Sheriff's Office. Deputies arrived at 3:10 a.m., and {D} left with them without any trouble. I had no physical contact with {D} at any point.\""), .cross("The freezing rain alert was in effect that night, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. There was an alert, and it was sleeting when I went out for my break. I won't pretend it was pleasant weather to be standing on a curb.\""), .cross("Did {D} ever ask for medical attention or say {D.he} felt sick?", "\"No. {D} said nothing about being ill. If I had heard that, I would have walked {D.him} to triage.\""), .cross("Was another waiting area open that night?", "\"There is a small chapel lobby on the first floor, but it's locked after nine. I did not offer it, and I did not check with a supervisor about alternatives.\""), .cross("Did {D} cause any disturbance while sitting there?", "\"No. {D} was quiet, took up one chair, and did not bother any patients. My only issue was that {D} had no reason on the registry to be there.\""), .cross("Did you offer {D} help finding a ride or a shelter?", "\"I mentioned a shelter once, but I did not call anyone for {D}. I told {D.him} to wait outside. I didn't have a number for a shelter handy.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Hospital volunteer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do at the hospital?", "\"I volunteer at the information desk at the emergency entrance, evenings and some overnights. I help visitors find rooms and offer coffee.\""), .direct("Were you there the night of {DATE}?", "\"Yes. I was on until about one in the morning, and I remember the sleet because it was hammering the glass doors of the lobby.\""), .direct("Did you notice {D} in the waiting room?", "\"I saw someone in a chair near the vending machines with a jacket over {D.his} shoulders. {D} looked cold and tired. {D} wasn't bothering anybody.\""), .direct("Did you speak with {D}?", "\"Briefly, around eleven thirty. I asked if {D} needed anything and {D} said {D.he} was waiting for a ride and would be fine. I offered a coffee and {D} declined.\""), .direct("What was the weather like?", "\"Freezing rain, with an alert on the screen. The roads were slick, and a couple of patients came in with minor crashes.\""), .direct("Do other people sometimes wait in the lobby until morning?", "\"It happens. Families wait for news, and sometimes people wait out bad weather. The guards usually decide case by case.\""), .cross("Did you hear the guard ask {D} to leave?", "\"I was gone by one, so I only could have heard the midnight request. I do not recall the exact words, and I was not near them.\""), .cross("Did you know whether {D} had a patient in the building?", "\"No. I assumed not because {D} told me {D.he} was waiting for a ride, but I never looked at any registry.\""), .cross("Is there a posted policy about overnight stays?", "\"Yes. A sign near the triage window says patients and escorts only overnight. I've read it many times.\""), .cross("Did you tell {D} {D.he} could stay?", "\"No. I am a volunteer and I do not have that authority. I only said hello and offered coffee.\""), .cross("Did {D} tell you whether the ride was on its way?", "\"{D} said it was coming. I have no way of knowing whether that was true.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} stayed after two warnings.", "{D} was waiting for a ride in bad weather."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had no ride and planned to sleep until morning.", "The shelter was full that night."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you go to the emergency waiting room that night?", "\"The weather turned to freezing rain right as I was walking, and the hospital was the nearest building with its lights on. I needed to get inside and out of the sleet.\""), .direct("What were you waiting for?", "\"A ride. I had texted someone and was told they would come when the roads were safe. I figured it would be an hour or two, and I sat down to wait.\""), .direct("What did the guard say to you at midnight?", "\"The guard told me about the patients-only policy and asked me to leave. I said I was waiting on a ride and asked if I could stay until it came.\""), .direct("Why did you stay after the second warning?", "\"It was still sleeting, and I felt unsafe standing on the road. I thought if I stayed quiet and out of the way, it would not hurt anyone.\""), .direct("How did you feel when deputies arrived?", "\"Embarrassed, mostly. I got up, got my jacket, and walked out with them. I did not argue, and I didn't understand why it was a crime.\""), .direct("Where did you go after that?", "\"The deputies gave me a ride to the corner of town, and I walked to a friend's. By then the rain had mostly stopped.\""), .cross("You were told twice to leave, weren't you?", "\"Yes, at about midnight and again at two. I heard both requests and understood them. I chose to stay, and I knew the policy at that point.\""), .cross("You were asleep for part of that time, weren't you?", "\"I dozed on and off. I didn't sleep through the whole thing. I was trying to stay awake in case my ride called.\""), .cross("You didn't have a patient inside, did you?", "\"No. I wasn't there to see anyone or to be seen. I only needed shelter from the weather.\""), .cross("Did your ride ever come?", "\"Not while I was at the hospital. I'm not going to say more than that about it, because I don't want to guess about what happened with that ride.\""), .cross("You could have waited at a bus shelter or the entrance vestibule, couldn't you?", "\"The vestibule was colder than the street because of the doors. I didn't think of the bus shelter, which is about a block away.\"")],
        openings: ("The hospital's policy is posted: only patients and escorts may stay overnight in the emergency waiting room. {D} had neither, was asked to leave at midnight and again at two, and stayed in the chair until deputies came at 3:10. The camera and the guard's account fit together.", "It was a freezing rain night, and {D} did what a cold person would do, which was sit in a lit, public waiting room until a ride came. {D} was quiet, took one chair, and left peacefully with deputies. You will hear a volunteer who saw {D} that night."),
        closings: ("Two warnings, two refusals, and three hours in a chair after being told to go. The policy was posted and the guard was polite both times. {D} chose to stay, and that is what the law forbids.", "{D} caused no disturbance and harmed no patient, and sleet was hammering the doors. No one offered a shelter, an alternative waiting area, or a call to anyone. The State has not shown that {D} stayed in defiance rather than out of the weather."),
        timeline: [(0, "11:20 p.m.: {D} settles into a chair."), (0, "Midnight: the first warning."), (0, "2 a.m.: the second warning."), (0, "3:10 a.m.: deputies arrive.")],
        identified: "The waiting room camera identifies {D}.",
        notDone: ["The shelter's capacity that night was never confirmed.", "The guard was never asked whether another waiting area was open."],
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let barBannedV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.barBanned",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Sports Bar Patron Returns for Trivia Night After Emailed Ban", "Manager Says Banned Customer Came Back Two Weeks Later"],
        law: "trespass2",
        spec: "Entered and remained on the premises of {V}, a sports bar, after being notified not to, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "A sports bar manager emailed {D} a trespass notice two weeks before {DATE} after a broken pitcher and a fight. At 8:45 p.m. on {DATE}, {D} came back for trivia night and took a table. The manager asked {D} to leave and {D} refused until deputies came at 9:10 p.m. {D} says {D.he} never opened the email.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Trespass Email", "An emailed notice to {D}'s address with a read receipt at 2:12 a.m. the day after it was sent."), E(.video, 2, "Bar Camera", "{D} takes a table at 8:45 p.m. and stays through two requests to leave."), E(.statement, 2, "Manager", "Asked {DL} twice to leave and was told {D.he} had a right to be there."), E(.document, 2, "Deputy's Report", "Deputies arrived at 9:10 p.m. and {D} left with them.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Never Opened", "{DL} says {D.he} never opened the email and did not know of the ban."), E(.document, 1, "Inbox Screenshot", "A screenshot with the message unread and a different date.")],
        role: "Sports bar manager",
        exam: [.direct("What is your role at the sports bar?", "\"I'm the general manager. I run the floor, hire the servers, and decide who is welcome. On {DATE} I was working trivia night.\""), .direct("Why was {D} not welcome at the bar?", "\"About two weeks earlier there was a fight at one of our tables, and {D} was involved when a pitcher was broken. I decided to ban {D} and put it in writing.\""), .direct("How did you notify {D} of the ban?", "\"I emailed a trespass notice to the address on {D}'s loyalty account. The email system logged a read receipt at 2:12 a.m. the day after I sent it.\""), .direct("What did you see on the night of {DATE}?", "\"At 8:45 p.m. {D} came in for trivia night and sat down at a table near the back. I recognized {D} on the floor right away.\""), .direct("What did you say to {D}?", "\"I walked up, told {D} the notice had been sent and that {D} was no longer allowed in, and asked {D.him} to leave. {D} said {D.he} had a right to be there.\""), .direct("How did the situation end?", "\"I asked a second time and got the same answer, so I called the Sheriff's Office. Deputies arrived at 9:10, and {D} left with them.\""), .cross("Did you ever hand {D} a paper notice or tell {D} in person?", "\"No. The email was the only notice I sent. I did not speak with {D} between the fight and trivia night.\""), .cross("Who else was at the table when the pitcher broke?", "\"Three or four people. I only banned {D} because I saw {D.him} swing. I did not ban the others.\""), .cross("Is the loyalty email address current?", "\"I do not know when {D} last updated it. The system showed that address on the account, so I used it.\""), .cross("Did you post anything at the door about banned patrons?", "\"We have a sign about the right to refuse service. I did not post a name list, and I can't point to any sign that names {D}.\""), .cross("Did {D} threaten anyone when asked to leave?", "\"No. {D} was loud and insisted on a right to stay, but there was no threat. {D} left peacefully with the deputies.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Server at trivia night",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What was your job at the bar?", "\"I'm a server. I work trivia night most weeks, so I was on the floor on {DATE}, taking drink orders for the teams.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} come in?", "\"Yes. {D} walked in at about a quarter to nine and joined a team at a table near the back. {D} looked excited and ordered a pitcher of water.\""), .direct("How did {D} act when the manager approached?", "\"Confused, honestly. {D} looked up and asked what the manager meant. {D} did not seem to know why {D.he} was being asked to go.\""), .direct("Did you hear what the manager said?", "\"Something about a notice that went out by email. {D} said {D.he} had not seen it, and the manager said that was not the bar's problem.\""), .direct("Did {D} argue loudly?", "\"Some, as it went on. But {D} never got physical or threatening. {D} left with the deputies without a hand laid on {D.him}.\""), .direct("Did you know {D} had been banned?", "\"No. Nobody told the servers about it. If I had known I would have said something at the door.\""), .cross("Were you working the night of the fight?", "\"I was off. I only know about it from coworkers and what the manager told staff afterward.\""), .cross("Did you see the email notice?", "\"No. I do not have access to the manager's email, and I never saw it printed or posted anywhere.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} read the email?", "\"No. I never saw {D} with a phone out at that table, and I cannot speak to what {D} read or did not read.\""), .cross("Are you friends with {D}?", "\"I know {D} as a regular customer. We are friendly, but I'm here to say what I saw, not to take sides.\""), .cross("Did the manager ask {D} to leave twice?", "\"Yes, I believe the manager asked twice before calling the deputies. {D} said no both times.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} returned despite a notice of the ban.", "{D} never saw the notice."),
        allocution: "\"I'm sorry for the trouble I caused.\"",
        truths: ("The read receipt shows {DL}'s device opened the notice.", "The email went to an old loyalty address."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you go to the bar on {DATE}?", "\"Trivia night is a long-time tradition with my friends, and my team had been practicing all week. I had no idea I wasn't welcome.\""), .direct("Were you involved in the fight a couple of weeks earlier?", "\"I was at the table, and a pitcher got broken in the commotion. I thought it was settled when the staff cleaned it up, and nobody said anything to me that night.\""), .direct("Did you know about the ban?", "\"No. The first I heard of it was when the manager came to my table. Nobody called, nobody texted, nobody handed me anything.\""), .direct("What about the email?", "\"I rarely look at the loyalty address. I only use it for coupons, and it fills up. I had no clue there was a notice sitting in it.\""), .direct("Why did you refuse to leave at first?", "\"Because it made no sense to me. I told the manager I had a right to be there, since nobody had ever told me otherwise.\""), .direct("What did you do once deputies came?", "\"I walked out with them, calmly. I told them I never saw the notice, and I showed them my inbox as soon as I could.\""), .cross("The read receipt shows the message was opened, doesn't it?", "\"The receipt says that, I've been told. I don't know how that could be, and I don't remember opening it. I will not guess about that.\""), .cross("You do remember the fight, don't you?", "\"Yes, I remember the fight, and I remember the broken pitcher. I knew it was serious. I did not think it meant I'd been banned.\""), .cross("You were asked to leave twice and stayed, weren't you?", "\"Yes. I stayed because I did not think I was doing anything wrong. In hindsight, I should have just left and sorted it out.\""), .cross("The manager told you the notice had been sent, didn't the manager?", "\"Yes, the manager said an email had been sent. That is the first time I heard it, and I was surprised.\""), .cross("Your inbox screenshot shows a different date, doesn't it?", "\"It shows the message unread, with a date that doesn't line up with the notice. I can't explain why, but that is what is on my screen.\"")],
        openings: ("Two weeks after a broken pitcher and a fight, the manager emailed {D} a trespass notice, and the read receipt shows it was opened the next morning. On trivia night, {D} walked in anyway, was asked twice to leave, and stayed until deputies came. The bar camera shows each step.", "{D} never saw the email, which went to an old loyalty address, and nobody called or handed {D} a paper notice. A regular walked in for trivia night, confused about why the manager was upset. You will hear from a server who watched it unfold."),
        closings: ("The notice went to {D}'s address, a read receipt shows it was opened, and the manager asked twice in person. {D} stayed at the table until deputies arrived at 9:10. That is a return after notice and a refusal to leave.", "A read receipt tells you an inbox was opened, not who opened it or whether anyone read the words. No one handed {D} a paper, posted a sign, or called. The State has not proved {D} knew about the ban."),
        timeline: [(-14, "The manager emails {D} the trespass notice."), (0, "8:45 p.m.: {D} takes a table at trivia night."), (0, "9:10 p.m.: deputies arrive."), (1, "The bar sends the email and its read receipt.")],
        identified: "The manager recognized {D}, and the read receipt ties the notice to {D}'s address.",
        notDone: ["The read receipt was never tied to {DL}'s own device.", "The bar's door sign about banned patrons was never produced."],
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let burnoutLotV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.burnoutLot",
        category: .traffic,
        headlines: ["Driver Spins Tires Through Farmers Market Lot as Vendors Pack Up", "Market Vendors Dive Behind Stalls as Car Circles"],
        law: "recklessDriving",
        spec: "Drove carelessly and heedlessly in willful disregard of the rights and safety of others, spinning a car through a market parking lot, on {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A Saturday farmers market was packing up at 1:15 p.m. on {DATE}. {D} drove into the lot and spun the car in two wide circles within feet of vendors loading trucks. A vendor pulled a child out of the way. A deputy stopped {D} at 1:20 p.m. {D} says the lot looked empty from the road.",
        state: [E(.video, 3, "Market Camera", "{D}'s car circles twice near stalls while vendors load trucks."), E(.statement, 3, "Vendor", "Pulled a child away as the car spun past."), E(.document, 2, "Tire Marks Photos", "Two black arcs across the lot near the loading area."), E(.document, 2, "Deputy's Report", "Stopped {D} at 1:20 p.m. with the smell of burned rubber.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Empty Lot", "{DL} says the lot looked empty from the road."), E(.document, 1, "Lot Hours Sign", "A sign says the market ends at 1 p.m.")],
        role: "Market vendor",
        exam: [.direct("What do you sell at the farmers market?", "\"I run a produce stand selling vegetables and cut flowers. I was there on {DATE} and we were loading trucks after the one o'clock close.\""), .direct("What was happening in the lot at about 1:15?", "\"Vendors were breaking down tents and backing trucks up to their stalls. There were people carrying crates, and a few kids helping their parents near the loading area.\""), .direct("What did you see {D}'s car do?", "\"A car came into the lot from the road at speed and spun in two wide circles in front of the loading area, squealing and throwing up smoke, only a few feet from us.\""), .direct("How close did it get to people?", "\"Within a few feet of me and a neighboring vendor. One of the vendors grabbed a child and pulled the child out of the way as the car swung by.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I got my own child behind my truck, called out to the others, and someone called the Sheriff's Office. A deputy stopped {D} about five minutes later.\""), .direct("What marks were left in the lot?", "\"Two black arcs across the asphalt near the loading area. A deputy photographed them. They were very fresh, and the smell of burned rubber hung over the lot.\""), .cross("The market ended at one o'clock, didn't it?", "\"Yes. The sign at the entrance says one. But many of us are still loading for another half hour, and that is common knowledge.\""), .cross("Could {D} see the loading area from the road?", "\"I'm not sure. My truck and a few others were parked along the edge and may have blocked some of the view. I can't say what {D} saw.\""), .cross("Did the car actually hit anyone or anything?", "\"No. It missed us and our trucks. Nobody was hurt and nothing was damaged.\""), .cross("Was there a guard at the entrance?", "\"There is usually someone at the gate during market hours. I did not see what that person said to {D}, if anything.\""), .cross("How long did the spinning last?", "\"Maybe ten seconds, maybe fifteen. It was fast. It felt longer because it was so loud.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Other market vendor",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What did you sell at the market?", "\"I sell eggs and honey. I was loading my truck at the far end on {DATE}, and my truck was one of several parked along the edge of the lot.\""), .direct("Where were the trucks positioned?", "\"In a line along the edge near the road, with the rear ends facing the stalls. They made a kind of wall between the road and the loading area.\""), .direct("Could someone driving by see the loading area?", "\"Not well. From the road you mostly see truck cabs and the side panels. People are on the far side, behind the trucks.\""), .direct("What did you see of {D}'s car?", "\"I heard tires squealing and looked up to see a car spinning near the middle of the lot. It happened fast and then it was gone.\""), .direct("What was the market's closing time?", "\"One o'clock. But vendors keep loading until about one thirty, and the gate stays open. Nobody puts out cones or closes it.\""), .direct("Was anyone at the gate that day?", "\"There was a volunteer at the entrance earlier, but I did not see anyone there after one. I could not say what was said to anyone.\""), .cross("Did you see anyone nearly get hit?", "\"I heard that a child was pulled away, but I did not see it myself. I was at my truck, turned the other way.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} look at the vendors?", "\"I couldn't see inside the car. I have no idea what {D} was looking at.\""), .cross("Would you say the lot was empty?", "\"No. There were people loading, and a few of us still working. It was not empty.\""), .cross("Did you hear anyone call out to {D}?", "\"Several people were yelling after it started. Before that, I did not hear anyone try to warn {D}.\""), .cross("Do you know {D}?", "\"No, I'd never seen {D} before that day. I only know what I saw of the car and the truck line.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} spun a car through a crowded lot.", "The lot looked empty."),
        allocution: "\"I'll never do that again.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had been told by a security guard the market was still open.", "The vendors' trucks blocked the view from the road."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you drive into the market lot that afternoon?", "\"I thought it was an empty lot. I was on my way somewhere, saw the wide open pavement from the road, and pulled in on impulse.\""), .direct("What did you see from the road?", "\"A big stretch of asphalt with a few trucks on the far side. I did not see people from where I was, because the trucks along the edge blocked the view.\""), .direct("What did you do in the lot?", "\"I spun the car around twice. It was a stupid thing to do. I thought nobody was there to see it.\""), .direct("Did you see people?", "\"Not until I was already turning. Then I saw some people near the trucks, and I stopped and drove out.\""), .direct("Did anyone tell you the market was still open?", "\"I'd rather say only what I'm sure of. I remember someone near the entrance saying something, but I wasn't paying attention to what.\""), .direct("What happened with the deputy?", "\"I pulled over on the road about a minute later, and the deputy came up. I told the deputy exactly what I did and said I was sorry.\""), .cross("The camera shows vendors loading trucks, doesn't it?", "\"It does. I can see that now. I did not notice them at the time because of the angle.\""), .cross("You spun the car twice, didn't you?", "\"Yes, twice. It was deliberate in that I turned the wheel and hit the gas. I did not intend to endanger anyone.\""), .cross("You came in fast, didn't you?", "\"I came in with some speed, yes. I was aiming to spin, so I had to build speed. It was reckless of me.\""), .cross("The entrance sign says the market ends at one, doesn't it?", "\"Yes, and it was after one. That made me think the lot would be empty. It was a mistake to trust that.\""), .cross("A child was pulled out of the way, wasn't a child?", "\"That's what the vendor says, and I have to take that seriously. I feel terrible about that. I didn't see it.\"")],
        openings: ("The farmers market ended at one, but vendors were still loading trucks at 1:15 when {D} drove into the lot and spun the car in two wide circles feet from them. A vendor pulled a child out of the way. The market camera and the tire marks tell the story.", "{D} saw what looked like an empty lot from the road, with a row of vendor trucks blocking the view of the loading area. {D} did something foolish, saw the people, and stopped. You will hear a vendor explain how those trucks blocked the view."),
        closings: ("The sign said one o'clock, and every person who sells there knows the loading goes on after that. {D} spun a car twice within a few feet of vendors and a child. The video, the arcs on the pavement, and the smell of rubber leave no doubt.", "The trucks formed a wall between the road and the loading area, and {D} stopped as soon as the people came into view. {D} told the deputy everything and apologized. The State must prove {D} knew people were in danger and acted anyway."),
        timeline: [(0, "1:00 p.m.: the market ends."), (0, "1:15 p.m.: {D}'s car circles the lot."), (0, "1:20 p.m.: the deputy stops {D}."), (1, "The market sends its camera video.")],
        identified: "The deputy stopped {D} minutes after the market camera recorded the spin.",
        notDone: ["The security guard's warning was never confirmed.", "The vendors' truck positions were never mapped."],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])
}
